text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', 'Add {B}{B}{B}.', 'As Quirion Elves enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\n{T}: Add one mana of the chosen color.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, discard a card at random.\\nSonic Burst deals 4 damage to any target.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, target non-Wall creature an opponent controls gains forestwalk until your next upkeep. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Bloodrock Cyclops attacks each combat if able.', 'Choose one —\\n• Thunderbolt deals 3 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\n• Thunderbolt deals 4 damage to target creature with flying.', "Clockwork Beast enters the battlefield with seven +1/+0 counters on it.\\nAt end of combat, if Clockwork Beast attacked or blocked this combat, remove a +1/+0 counter from it.\\n{X}, {T}: Put up to X +1/+0 counters on Clockwork Beast. This ability can't cause the total number of +1/+0 counters on Clockwork Beast to be greater than seven. Activate only during your upkeep.", "Counter target spell unless its controller pays {X}. If that player doesn't, they tap all lands with mana abilities they control and lose all unspent mana.", 'Counter target spell.', "Destroy target nonartifact, nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target tapped creature.', 'Discard all the cards in your hand, then draw that many cards.', 'Draw three cards, then put two cards from your hand on top of your library in any order.', 'Dwarven Ruins enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Dwarven Ruins: Add {R}{R}.', 'Ebon Stronghold enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Ebon Stronghold: Add {B}{B}.', 'Enchant creature\\nPrevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by enchanted creature.', 'Enchant land\\nWhenever enchanted land is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional {G}.', 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhen Fog Elemental attacks or blocks, sacrifice it at end of combat.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Sengir Vampire this turn dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Sengir Vampire.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{R}: Shivan Dragon gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", "Flying\\nClockwork Avian enters the battlefield with four +1/+0 counters on it.\\nAt end of combat, if Clockwork Avian attacked or blocked this combat, remove a +1/+0 counter from it.\\n{X}, {T}: Put up to X +1/+0 counters on Clockwork Avian. This ability can't cause the total number of +1/+0 counters on Clockwork Avian to be greater than four. Activate only during your upkeep.", 'Flying\\nCloud Djinn can block only creatures with flying.', 'Flying\\nCloud Elemental can block only creatures with flying.', 'Flying\\nSacrifice a creature: Fallen Angel gets +2/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhen you cast a creature spell, sacrifice Skittering Skirge.', 'Flying\\n{2}{U}: Untap Vigilant Drake.', 'Flying\\n{3}{U}: Untap Blizzard Elemental.', "Flying\\n{U}: Put Wayward Soul on top of its owner's library.", 'Haste', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', 'Havenwood Battleground enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Havenwood Battleground: Add {G}{G}.', "Hulking Cyclops can't block.", 'Kird Ape gets +1/+2 as long as you control a Forest.', 'Lava Axe deals 5 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'Lightning Bolt deals 3 damage to any target.', 'Look at the top five cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest on top of your library in any order.', 'Look at the top four cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', 'Polluted Mire enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', "Put any number of target creature cards from your graveyard on top of your library.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nWhenever Woolly Spider blocks a creature with flying, Woolly Spider gets +0/+2 until end of turn.', 'Remote Isle enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Shock deals 2 damage to any target.', "Shroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'Slippery Karst enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Smoldering Crater enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R}.\\nCycling {2} ({2}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', "Spend only black mana on X.\\nDrain Life deals X damage to any target. You gain life equal to the damage dealt, but not more life than the player's life total before the damage was dealt, the planeswalker's loyalty before the damage was dealt, or the creature's toughness.", 'Svyelunite Temple enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Svyelunite Temple: Add {U}{U}.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Target player sacrifices a creature.', 'This spell costs {1} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nFireball deals X damage divided evenly, rounded down, among any number of targets.', 'Trample', "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, Force of Nature deals 8 damage to you unless you pay {G}{G}{G}{G}.", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nHaste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nAt the beginning of the end step, sacrifice Ball Lightning.", "Trample\\nLeviathan enters the battlefield tapped and doesn't untap during your untap step.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may sacrifice two Islands. If you do, untap Leviathan.\\nLeviathan can't attack unless you sacrifice two Islands. (This cost is paid as attackers are declared.)", 'When Balduvian Horde enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you discard a card at random.', 'When Gravedigger enters the battlefield, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Tar Pit Warrior becomes the target of a spell or ability, sacrifice it.', 'When you cast a creature spell, sacrifice Skittering Horror.', 'Whenever Crashing Boars attacks, defending player chooses an untapped creature they control. That creature blocks Crashing Boars this turn if able.', 'Whenever Hollow Dogs attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Segmented Wurm becomes the target of a spell or ability, put a -1/-1 counter on it.', '{R}{G}: Shambling Strider gets +1/-1 until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {G}.', "{U}: Giant Crab gains shroud until end of turn. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", '{U}: Killer Whale gains flying until end of turn.']
flavor: ['"Angels are simply extensions of truth upon the fabric of life—and there is far more dark than light."\\n—Baron Sengir', '"Catch!"', '"Controlling time ensures you need never look impulsive again."\\n—Teferi', '"Faugh!" snorted Tahngarth. "Why would it make a meal of something like you?" Squee looked relieved. "No," he continued, "you\'d make a much better toothpick."', '"Flourishing during the Ice Age, these wurms were the bane of all Kjeldorans. Their great size and ferocity made them the subject of countless nightmares—they embodied the worst of the Ice Age."\\n—*Kjeldor: Ice Civilization*', '"He\'s big an\' dumb an\' ready to fight. A lot like ol\' Hornhead here."\\n—Squee, goblin cabin hand, scouting report', '"I have seen the true path. I will not warm myself by the fire—I will become the flame."\\n—Lim-Dûl, the Necromancer', '"I reeled from the blow, and then suddenly, I knew exactly what to do. Within moments victory was mine."\\n—Gustha Ebbasdotter\\nKjeldoran royal mage', '"I\'ve seen fog so thick you could cut it, but none that could cut me."\\n—Tahngarth of the *Weatherlight*', '"If only we could so easily leave behind those parts of ourselves that pain us."\\n—Crovax', '"It\'s hard to hurt anyone when you\'re as transparent as your motives."\\n—Ertai, wizard adept', '"Most wizards consider a thunderbolt to be a proper retort."\\n—Ertai, wizard adept', '"Only fools believe they will face my armies but once."\\n—Kaervek', '"The cyclops shrugged off savage blows, but casual insults made him weep."\\n—Azeworai, "The Cyclops who Couldn\'t"', '"The nightstalkers are such a minor power in Urborg. Their sad eagerness to elevate themselves makes them willing tools in the plundering of little Femeref."\\n—Kaervek', '"There\'s very little that escapes me, Greven. And you will escape very little if you fail."\\n—Volrath', '"This monstrosity will do—for now."\\n—Davvol, Evincar of Rath', '"We need not fear the forces of the air; I\'ve yet to see a spider without an appetite."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, elvish hunter', '"When traveling the Great Desert avoid wearing the scales of lizards, for the Viashino rule the sands and look poorly on the skinning of their cousins."\\n—Zhalfirin Guide to the Desert', '"You know you\'ve angered the gods when the clouds turn against you."\\n—Sisay, Captain of the *Weatherlight*', '"no home no heart no hope"\\n—Stronghold graffito', 'A full coffin is like a full coffer—both are attractive to thieves.', 'A hollow dog is never empty. It is filled with thirst for the hunt.', "Afterward, Tolaria's winds were like the whispers of lost wizards, calling for life.", 'Anyone can get around a cyclops, but few can stand in its way.', "As elusive as the footprint of a djinn\\n—Suq'Ata expression", 'As insubstantial, and as powerful, as the wind that carries it.', 'Awake and awing in the blink of an eye.', 'Bores ruin a party. Boars are party to ruin.', "Don't insult a Talruum unless your mount is swift.\\n—Suq'Ata saying", 'Drakes claim to be dragons—until the dragons show up.', "During the giant crabs' mating season, Skyshroud nights are filled with the clatter of their skirmishes.", "For a sharp second, Selenia froze, and Crovax's blade found home, As the angel shattered like glass, Crovax felt his mind collapse—the curse had been fulfilled.", "Freyalise forbid that any stranger should wander into the striders' territory.", 'Greven *il*-Vec lifted Vhati off his feet. "The fall will give you time to think on your failure."', 'He raged at the world, at his family, at his life. But mostly he just raged.', 'Hunger is like the sea: deep, endless, and unforgiving.', 'Lightning tethers souls to the world.\\n—Kor saying', 'Love is like a rhino, short-sighted and hasty; if it cannot find a way, it will make a way.\\n—Femeref adage', "Most spiders wait patiently for their prey to arrive. Most spiders aren't forty feet tall.", 'Music scythes the savage beast.', 'Of royal blood among the spirits of the air, the Mahamoti djinn rides on the wings of the winds. As dangerous in the gambling hall as he is in battle, he is a master of trickery and misdirection.', 'One bone broken for every twig snapped underfoot.\\n—Llanowar penalty for trespassing', 'Rath forces plants from its surface as one presses whey from cheese.', 'Students who had seen Rayne argue with Urza were certain she had summoned it to make him seem warmer by comparison.', 'The giant was felt a few seconds before he was seen.', "The imps' warbling cries echo through Phyrexia's towers like those of mourning doves in a cathedral.", "When the gorilla playfully grabbed the wurm's tail, the wurm doubled back and playfully ate the gorilla's head.", 'With his newfound sense of self-importance, Squee set his sights on ever-bigger bugs.']
